TI  - Submental Intubation.
PG  - e1896
LID - 10.1097/GOX.0000000000001896 [doi]
LID - e1896
AB  - Acquisition of a secure airway is an essential element of the operative 
      management of maxillofacial trauma. Of the options available, submental 
      intubation is an alternative to tracheostomy. The access should be accomplished 
      via a midline approach rather than lateral through the mylohyoid, an armored 
      endotracheal tube utilized to prevent kinking, and the passage facilitated by use 
      of wound dilators obtained from a percutaneous tracheostomy set.
