TI  - Experimental model for percutaneous tracheostomy training.
PG  - 101612
LID - S1808-8694(25)00055-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.bjorl.2025.101612 [doi]
LID - 101612
AB  - OBJECTIVE: To propose a practical and accessible model that enables the training 
      of this technique. METHODS: The model comprises a structure composed of a wood 
      board resting on a PVC tube. A foam block on which the pig trachea is supported 
      is placed on this structure. A foam sheet covered with fabric is placed over the 
      trachea to simulate the soft parts of the neck and the skin. This is a practical 
      training model for practice of surgeons in percutaneous tracheostomy. A 
      questionnaire on the assessment of the proposed model to each participating 
      surgeon was applied. RESULTS: Ten surgeons underwent training on the model: two 
      experienced head and neck surgeons, three specialty residents, one 
      otorhinolaryngologist, and three general surgery residents. All of them were able 
      to perform the procedure successfully. CONCLUSION: The proposed simulation model 
      presented good results when applied to surgeons, and it is a possible alternative 
      to percutaneous tracheostomy training. LEVEL OF EVIDENCE: Level III.
