TI  - [Percutaneous tracheostomy].
PG  - 681-5
AB  - Percutaneous tracheostomy using dilatation is a new technique for opening up the 
      trachea whose use has become generalized in intensive care units since this 
      method has numerous advantages over conventional tracheostomy and a lesser number 
      of adverse effects. This article describes a nursing protocol for this technique; 
      it reviews its most frequent complications and it details the nursing care which 
      patients require once they have undergone.
