DP  - 2000 Aug
TI  - When and how should we do a tracheostomy?
PG  - 267-270
AB  - Tracheostomy is one of the most common surgical procedures in the intensive care 
      unit. Since the introduction of percutaneous techniques, tracheostomy has become 
      increasingly popular. The technique is relatively easy, and the early and late 
      complication rates are relatively low.It is unknown at which moment tracheostomy 
      can best be performed in the translaryngeally intubated patient. There are 
      theoretic arguments for both early and late tracheostomy. The excellent results 
      of percutaneous tracheostomy may influence the decision to perform a tracheostomy 
      rather early, but prospective randomized studies are required to gather the 
      necessary evidence.
