TI  - Insertion of percutaneous ECMO cannula.
PG  - 184-5
AB  - Extracorporeal membrane oxygenation plays a very important role in resuscitation 
      when patients are approaching impending death, because it can provide adequate 
      cardiac and pulmonary support immediately. But percutaneous tunnel creation is a 
      critical step for set-up of extracorporeal membrane oxygenation by percutaneous 
      Seldinger technique. A guidewire dilator forceps used in percutaneous 
      tracheostomy was tried to create the femoral subcutaneous tunnel. We found it 
      could make easy the advancement of the percutaneous cannula into the vessels and 
      over-dilatation of the vessels could also be prevented by controlled jaw opening.
