TI  - Ultrasound-guided tracheostomy--not for the many, but perhaps the few... or the 
      one.
PG  - 147
LID - 10.1186/cc10106 [doi]
AB  - Percutaneous tracheostomy has become a routine procedure in most intensive care 
      units, and point of care ultrasound is becoming used with greater frequency to 
      augment diagnosis and therapy for critically ill patients. The case series from 
      Rajajee and colleagues incorporates 'real-time' ultrasound in an effort to 
      improve the safety of percutaneous tracheostomy. While their report does not 
      prove that ultrasound should be used prior to or during all percutaneous 
      tracheostomies, it does reinforce several important safety considerations 
      concerning the anatomy of the neck, and in particular the potential to encounter 
      bleeding complications during these procedures.
