TI  - Revision Tracheotomy Complicated by History of Follicular B-Cell Lymphoma.
PG  - 16S-19S
LID - 10.1177/01455613231189229 [doi]
AB  - This case report presents a 65-year-old woman with multiple complications during 
      a revision tracheotomy including subcutaneous emphysema and a pneumothorax. 
      Management of her airway was complicated by a history of recurrent follicular 
      B-cell lymphoma associated with extensive cervical lymphadenopathy. We detail the 
      importance of heightened clinical awareness and the use of intraoperative safety 
      adjuncts when performing revision tracheostomies.
