TI  - Complications of percutaneous tracheostomy.
PG  - 1282-3
AB  - Percutaneous tracheostomy is a technique that, reputedly, is simple to perform 
      and causes few complications. It is routinely used in intensive care. We present 
      two patients with tracheal stenosis. In one patient, we had to perform an 
      anastomotic resection to cure the patient; in the other patient, we had to place 
      an endoluminal conformer. To our knowledge, this complication has not been 
      reported in association with the use of this technique.
