TI  - Fatal Acute Airway Obstruction During Bronchoscopy-Guided Percutaneous 
      Tracheostomy: An Analysis of a New Complication.
PG  - e43593
LID - 10.7759/cureus.43593 [doi]
LID - e43593
AB  - Percutaneous tracheostomy (PT) is a commonly performed procedure in ICUs as a 
      safe and cost-effective alternative to surgical tracheostomy (ST). Bronchoscopy 
      is frequently used during PT for real-time confirmation of needle placement and 
      tube positioning. We present a case of a 42-year-old female with a complex 
      medical history who underwent PT and experienced acute airway loss due to 
      endotracheal tube obstruction caused by accumulated secretions. To prevent such 
      complications, vigilance regarding airway obstruction, cautious bronchoscope 
      advancement, avoiding endotracheal tube puncture, and readiness to abort the 
      procedure and replace the tube are crucial.
