TI  - Safe tracheostomy: blunt puncture and dilation after minimal surgical exposure of 
      the trachea (BPAD tracheostomy).
PG  - 773-6
LID - 10.1002/ccr3.340 [doi]
AB  - A number of complications can occur following both surgical tracheostomy (ST) and 
      percutaneous tracheostomy (PT). A flexible new tracheostomy insertion technique 
      with the advantages of both ST and PT is proposed to reduce these complications. 
      Our blunt puncture and dilation technique (BPAD tracheostomy) appears to be 
      technically safe and feasible to perform.
