TI  - A Modified Tracheostomy Technique in an Adult Patient With Klippel-Feil Syndrome.
PG  - e70532
LID - 10.1002/ccr3.70532 [doi]
LID - e70532
AB  - Placing a tracheostomy is challenging in patients with Klippel-Feil syndrome due 
      to a short, flexed, and immobile neck that can limit surgical access to the 
      trachea. Here, we report a modified technique with elements from both open and 
      percutaneous tracheostomy without requiring sternotomy.
