IS  - 2213-0071 (Electronic)
IS  - 2213-0071 (Linking)
VI  - 16
DP  - 2015
TI  - Is percutaneous tracheostomy the best method in the management of patients with 
      prolonged mechanical ventilation?
PG  - 69-70
LID - 10.1016/j.rmcr.2015.07.008 [doi]
AB  - Although percutaneous tracheostomy is a standardized procedure, rare major 
      complications are still being evaluated and discussed. We describe a case of 
      patient, with hemodynamic and respiratory stability, who displayed massive 
      hemorrhage after 16 days of "Ciaglia Blue Rhino" tracheostomy. Unfortunately, 
      neither prompt resuscitation maneuvers nor the surgical approach saved the life 
      of patient.
