PMID- 15747510
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 20050401
LR  - 20061115
IS  - 0021-4892 (Print)
IS  - 0021-4892 (Linking)
VI  - 54
IP  - 2
DP  - 2005 Feb
TI  - [Percutaneous tracheostomy to the patient with coagulopathy].
PG  - 153-5
AB  - BACKGROUND: Generally, coagulopathy is a relative contraindication for surgical 
      tracheotomy. METHODS: Fourteen patients with severe respiratory failure and 
      coagulopathy underwent elective percutaneous tracheostomy using Portex 
      percutaneous tracheostomy kit. RESULTS: Apart from minor bleeding episodes during 
      and after the procedures which were controlled promptly, no other complications 
      occurred. CONCLUSIONS: If careful precautions are observed, we believe that 
      percutaneous tracheostomy is safe even in patients with severe respiratory 
      failure and coagulopathy.
