PMID- 11094677
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 20010301
LR  - 20190319
IS  - 0310-057X (Print)
IS  - 0310-057X (Linking)
VI  - 28
IP  - 5
DP  - 2000 Oct
TI  - Tracheo-innominate fistula after initial percutaneous tracheostomy.
PG  - 566-9
AB  - We report a tracheo-innominate fistula formation after tracheostomy in a 
      68-year-old man with Guillain-Barré syndrome. The initial percutaneous 
      tracheostomy had to be revised surgically after the tube dislodged from its 
      insertion site in the trachea. Three days later, massive bleeding occurred and 
      emergency surgery revealed a fistula. This was surgically repaired but 
      subsequently re-bled with a fatal outcome. The post mortem report found an 
      aneurysmal ectatic innominate artery with a fistula involving the anterior 
      tracheal wall. The aetiology, diagnosis and management of tracheo-innominate 
      fistula are discussed.
