PMID- 15212135
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 20041018
LR  - 20220311
IS  - 0730-2347 (Print)
IS  - 0730-2347 (Linking)
VI  - 31
IP  - 2
DP  - 2004
TI  - Emergency percutaneous tracheostomy after unsuccessful orotracheal intubation in 
      a patient with an acute myocardial infarction.
PG  - 184-5
AB  - A 41-year-old woman had acute respiratory failure related to a myocardial 
      infarction. Attempts at orotracheal intubation were unsuccessful; therefore, an 
      emergency percutaneous tracheostomy was performed. The patient was then taken to 
      the cardiac catheterization laboratory for myocardial revascularization. After 
      the tracheostomy cannula was removed, the patient recovered successfully and was 
      discharged from the hospital. The percutaneous tracheostomy technique may be 
      useful in similar patients who need emergency airway access.
