TI  - A technical modification for percutaneous tracheostomy: prospective case series 
      study on one hundred patients.
PG  - 35
LID - 10.1186/1749-7922-6-35 [doi]
AB  - The purpose of this study is to describe a technical modification of percutaneous 
      tracheostomy that combines principles of the Percu Twist™ and the Griggs-Portex® 
      methods in a reusable kit. One hundred patients underwent the procedure. There 
      were no false passage, tube misplacement, or deaths related to the procedure. 
      There were two minor bleedings managed conservatively. The technical modification 
      described in this study is safe and simple to execute.
