DP  - 2017 Mar 15
TI  - Fiberoptic-Guided Blue Rhino Dilator-Assisted Dilation of Postintubation Tracheal 
      Stenosis: A Case Report About a Novel Technique.
PG  - 136-138
LID - 10.1213/XAA.0000000000000433 [doi]
AB  - Posttracheostomy tracheal stenosis is a rare complication of prolonged tracheal 
      intubation. Treatment modalities that may be used include surgical resection and 
      anastomosis, endoscopic tracheal dilation, laser resection, and tracheal 
      stenting. We describe a novel salvage modality for dilation of a symptomatic 
      tracheal stenosis using a percutaneous tracheostomy dilator wherein rigid 
      bronchoscopic dilation was not feasible and balloon tracheal dilation had failed.
