VI  - 7
IP  - 4
DP  - 2008 Aug
TI  - Graft repair of tracheo-innominate artery fistula following percutaneous 
      tracheostomy.
PG  - 654-5
LID - 10.1510/icvts.2007.174656 [doi]
AB  - Tracheo-innominate fistula (TIF) is a rare complication following percutaneous 
      dilatational tracheostomy (PDT), occurring in < or =1% of cases. It usually 
      develops three days to six weeks after the procedure and is fatal in the majority 
      of cases, even after successful initial repair. We present a successfully treated 
      case of TIF using a Goretex graft to replace the severely destroyed segment of 
      the innominate artery.
