VI  - 20
IP  - 4
DP  - 2001 Apr
TI  - [Difficult reintubation during a Fantoni's tracheostomy resolved using a 
      laryngeal mask].
PG  - 366-9
AB  - We report the failure of a reintubation under direct laryngoscopy, during a 
      percutaneous tracheostomy by Fantoni method. After the accidental per-procedural 
      extubation and in front of an unpredicted difficult conventional endotracheal 
      intubation, a laryngeal mask was used as an airway intubator conduit for the 
      blind passage of the set's ventilation tube. This ventilation tube is a 40 cm 
      long, 4 mm internal diameter special catheter with low pressure cuff, included 
      into the TLT kit. The end of the procedure was uneventful.
